Package: Rducksassy
Title: Approximate String Matching for 'DuckDB'
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Sounkou Mahamane", family = "Toure",
           email = "sounkoutoure@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person(given = "Rick", family = "Beeloo", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "Sassy, bundled under the MIT license"),
    person(given = "Ragnar", family = "Groot Koerkamp", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "Sassy, bundled under the MIT license"),
    person("DuckDB Foundation", role = "cph",
           comment = "DuckDB headers and metadata tool, bundled under the MIT license")
    )
Description: Builds and loads the 'ducksassy' extension for 'DuckDB', providing
    approximate DNA, IUPAC and ASCII string matching through the 'Sassy' SIMD
    kernels. Search scalar values, pattern panels and CRISPR guide targets from
    SQL. The matching method is described by Beeloo and Groot Koerkamp (2026)
    <doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btag244>.
License: GPL (>= 2)
Encoding: UTF-8
SystemRequirements: CMake (>= 3.20), Cargo (Rust's package manager) (>= 1.91),
    rustc (>= 1.91), Python (>= 3.8), C11 compiler
NeedsCompilation: yes
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports:
    DBI,
    duckdb (>= 1.5.5)
URL: https://github.com/RGenomicsETL/ducksassy,
    https://rgenomicsetl.github.io/ducksassy/
